---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data Disclaimer — SpecGrid"
  description="How SpecGrid compiles draft profiles, and how to claim, correct, or remove yours."
  canonicalPath="/data-disclaimer"
>
  <article class="doc-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="doc-header">
        <div class="titleblock" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <div>Document<strong>DOC-REF // DATA-DISCLAIMER-2026-08</strong></div>
          <div>Verification Tier<strong>Specification &amp; Status Tiers</strong></div>
          <div>Effective<strong>August 2026</strong></div>
          <div>Platform<strong>specgrid.in</strong></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tag" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">
          <span class="dot"></span>
          <span>Data Integrity &amp; Verification Tiers</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="doc-title">Data Disclaimer</h1>
        <div class="doc-meta mono">Last updated: August 2026</div>
        <p class="doc-lead">
          Many profiles on SpecGrid start as <strong>draft profiles</strong>: compiled from information the company has already made public (its own website, public directories, industry listings), before the company has reviewed or confirmed it.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="doc-content">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="doc-section">
          <div class="section-tag mono">§ 01 // Public Draft Scope</div>
          <h2>What this means</h2>
          <div class="tier-card">
            <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <span class="badge badge-draft">Draft Profile</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              A draft profile is our best attempt at an accurate summary — it is not verified by the company and may contain errors, outdated information, or gaps. It is clearly labeled "Draft profile" wherever it appears.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="doc-section">
          <div class="section-tag mono">§ 02 // Supplier Rights</div>
          <h2>If you are the company</h2>
          <p>
            You can: claim your profile to take control of it (edit specs, description, certifications directly), or request a correction or removal by emailing <a href="mailto:mathi@specgrid.in" class="doc-link">mathi@specgrid.in</a> — no verification hurdle required to have inaccurate information removed.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="doc-section">
          <div class="section-tag mono">§ 03 // Status Tiers &amp; Badges</div>
          <h2>Once claimed</h2>
          
          <div class="tiers-stack">
            <div class="tier-card">
              <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <span class="badge badge-verified">Verified</span>
              </div>
              <p>
                A "Verified" badge means SpecGrid manually reviewed the company (checked its LinkedIn presence, its own website, and the format of its GSTIN/CIN) — this is not a live government database check, since no free public GST/MCA verification API exists today; it is a manual, judgment-based check by SpecGrid.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="tier-card">
              <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <span class="badge" style="background: var(--paper-line); color: var(--ink);">Claimed</span>
              </div>
              <p>
                A "Claimed" badge means only that the claimant's work email matched the company's own listed website domain — no manual review has happened yet.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="tier-card">
              <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <span class="badge badge-founding">Founding Member</span>
              </div>
              <p>
                A "Founding member" badge is always manually reviewed. We will update this page if and when live government verification becomes part of the process.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="doc-section contact-panel">
          <div class="section-tag mono">§ 04 // Contact &amp; Updates</div>
          <h2>Questions or Corrections</h2>
          <p>
            If you need profile updates or have verification questions:
          </p>
          <div style="margin-top: 14px;">
            <a href="mailto:mathi@specgrid.in" class="btn btn-primary">
              <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="16" rx="2"/>
                <path d="m22 7-8.97 5.7a1.94 1.94 0 0 1-2.06 0L2 7"/>
              </svg>
              mathi@specgrid.in
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc-page {
    padding: 56px 0 72px;
  }

  .doc-header {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
    padding-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .doc-meta {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 680px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .doc-lead strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .doc-content {
    max-width: 720px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .doc-section {
    position: relative;
  }

  .section-tag {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--green);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .doc-section h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .doc-section p {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .tiers-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .tier-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
    background: var(--card);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .tier-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .doc-link {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .contact-panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
    background: var(--card);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
</style>
